# Core Feature Rules

## 1. Event Types
- Each event type must have: title, description, duration (minutes), and a unique URL slug
- Slug must be URL-safe: lowercase, hyphens only, no spaces — enforce with Zod regex
- Duplicate slug must return a `409 Conflict` response
- The public booking URL format is: `/[slug]`
- Deleting an event type must not delete past bookings — keep them intact

## 2. Availability
- Available days are stored as an array of weekday indices (0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday)
- Start time and end time are stored as `HH:mm` strings (e.g. `"09:00"`, `"17:00"`)
- Timezone is stored as an IANA timezone string (e.g. `"Asia/Kolkata"`)
- When calculating available slots, always subtract already-booked slots
- Slot generation: divide the available window into chunks equal to the event duration

## 3. Public Booking Page
- The booking page is fully public — no auth check
- Calendar must disable past dates and dates with no available slots
- Time slots must be displayed in the booker's local timezone (detect via `Intl.DateTimeFormat`)
- Booking form collects: full name, email — both required
- After successful booking, redirect to `/booking/confirmed?id=[bookingId]`
- Confirmation page must show: event title, date, time, duration, and booker name

## 4. Bookings Dashboard
- Separate tabs for "Upcoming" and "Past" bookings — split by current UTC time
- Each booking card shows: booker name, email, event title, date/time, and duration
- Cancel button must ask for confirmation before calling the cancel API
- Cancelled bookings should be visually distinct (muted, strikethrough, or a `CANCELLED` badge)
